    "content": "Released on April 2, 2008, *Blooddrunk* is Children of Bodom's sixth full-length album and a deliberate return to the aggressive, velocity-driven approach that defined their earlier work after the more commercially accessible *Are You Dead Yet?* (2005). Recorded at Sonic Pump Studios in Helsinki, Finland — a departure from the Astia Studio environment that had defined CoB's recording history — *Blooddrunk* marked the first time Anssi Kippo worked with the band in a different studio context, producing a drum sound with a new character while maintaining the musical intelligence of Raatikainen's playing.\n\nFor Jaska Raatikainen, *Blooddrunk* represented the Pearl Masters era fully established. The Pearl Masters Premium Maple shells, Zildjian A Custom and K Custom cymbals, and Pearl Eliminator double pedal that had debuted on *Are You Dead Yet?* were now a settled, familiar setup — the same gear foundation deployed across the CoB discography from this point forward. The result is a drum sound with the focused attack of Pearl's maple construction, the bright precision of Zildjian A Custom cymbals, and the aggressive double-kick capability of the Eliminator.\n\nTracks like \"Hellhounds on My Trail,\" \"Blooddrunk,\" and \"LoBodomy\" demonstrated the return to higher velocities and more demanding double-kick work compared to *Are You Dead Yet?*, while \"One Day You Will Cry\" showed the dynamic range the Pearl era setup could deliver across softer, more melodic passages. This article breaks down every component of Raatikainen's setup on *Blooddrunk* — the Pearl Masters shells, the Zildjian cymbal selection, the Pearl Eliminator, and the stylistic approach behind CoB's sixth studio record.",
