    "title": "Recording at Sonic Pump Studios: Kippo in a New Environment",
    "content": "*Blooddrunk* was the first Children of Bodom album recorded at Sonic Pump Studios in Helsinki — a significant departure from the Astia Studio, Imatra environment that had defined all previous CoB studio recordings with Anssi Kippo. The move brought a different acoustic profile to the sessions while preserving the Kippo production approach that had defined CoB's studio sound.\n\n**Sonic Pump vs. Astia Studio:**\nSonic Pump Studios' Helsinki location and larger recording spaces produced a drum sound with different natural room characteristics than Astia Studio's more controlled Imatra environment. Kippo's experience with Children of Bodom across multiple albums at Astia meant that adapting to Sonic Pump required careful attention to how the room's reflection character interacted with the Pearl Masters shells and the Zildjian cymbal setup. The result is a drum sound on *Blooddrunk* with a slightly different room character — audibly distinct from the Astia-era recordings, particularly in the way the kick drums and toms breathe in the room.\n\n**Return to Aggressive Tempos:**\nThe higher velocities and more demanding double-kick passages of *Blooddrunk* compared to *Are You Dead Yet?* required Kippo to return to the aggressive-tempo kick treatment approach of the *Follow the Reaper* and *Hate Crew Deathroll* sessions: EQ focused on the upper attack transient to maintain intelligibility during sustained double-bass patterns, with controlled low-end to prevent the kick from muddying the keyboard-heavy mix.\n\n**Pearl Masters Character in Sonic Pump's Acoustic:**\nThe Pearl Masters' more focused attack, combined with Sonic Pump's different reflective character, produced a drum sound with slightly more room dimension than the Astia recordings — the Pearl shells' controlled sustain interacting with the larger space in ways that Raatikainen's *Hatebreeder* and *Hate Crew Deathroll* recordings at Astia had not produced.",
